## Naming

`name` is the orb name **without** the namespace prefix — `node`, not `acme/node`. The namespace comes from `namespace_id`, and `full_name` is the computed `<namespace>/<orb>` reference.

Keeping the bare name separate is what makes the resource survive a namespace rename: renaming a `circleci_orb_namespace` changes `full_name`, but `name` is unchanged, so the orb is not replaced.

## What can and cannot be changed

| Attribute | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `is_listed` | In-place update, via the set-listed route. |
| `category_ids` | In-place update, via the add-category and remove-category routes. |
| `name`, `namespace_id`, `is_private` | Force a replacement — and since an orb cannot be deleted and its name is taken, the replacement's create will be rejected for `is_private`. Treat visibility as permanent. |

`category_ids` is deliberately optional and not computed. Omit it and the provider leaves categories alone, so categories set in the CircleCI UI are not removed behind your back. Set it — including to `[]` — and the provider reconciles the list exactly.

